  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The azo products obtained have an extended conjugate system having<br />both the aromatic rings joined through the &ndash;N=N&ndash; bond. These compounds<br />are often coloured and are used as dyes. The given diazonium salt couples with 1-naphthylamine&nbsp;to form a red azo-dye.&nbsp;This is an example of electrophilic substitution reaction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0064_3823ab1113ad.png\" style=\"width: 804px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
